DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       These functions compute the remainder and part of the quotient upon di‐
       vision  of  _x  by _y.  A few bits of the quotient are stored via the _q_u_o
       pointer.  The remainder is returned as the function result.

       The value of the remainder is the same as that computed by the  rreemmaaiinn‐‐
       ddeerr(3) function.

       The  value  stored via the _q_u_o pointer has the sign of _x _/ _y and agrees
       with the quotient in at least the low order 3 bits.

       For example, _r_e_m_q_u_o_(_2_9_._0_, _3_._0_) returns -1.0 and might  store  2.   Note
       that the actual quotient might not fit in an integer.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       On  success,  these  functions  return  the same value as the analogous
       functions described in rreemmaaiinnddeerr(3).

       If _x or _y is a NaN, a NaN is returned.

       If _x is an infinity, and _y is not a NaN, a domain error occurs,  and  a
       NaN is returned.

       If  _y  is zero, and _x is not a NaN, a domain error occurs, and a NaN is
       returned.

